the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    the Alter des Antragstellers of *a case* is *a number*; scenario element.
    Antragsteller volljährig holds for *a case*.
    Antragsteller volljährig would hold for *a case*; unknown.

the knowledge base r5_1_age_check includes:

the text of the_rulemap is at "sources/age-check.ruml".

Antragsteller volljährig holds for a case if
    the Alter des Antragstellers of the case is a number N
    and N >= 18.

Antragsteller volljährig holds for a case if
    it is not the case that the Alter des Antragstellers of the case is a number
    and Antragsteller volljährig would hold for the case.

scenario generated_1 is, as stated in "age-check.ruml" at generated_1:
    % every data point its first value
    the Alter des Antragstellers of case 1 is 18.
    node_1 expects answers ["Antragsteller volljährig holds for case 1"] and any unknowns.
    not_node_1 expects answers [].

scenario generated_2 is, as stated in "age-check.ruml" at generated_2:
    % dp_age has no value
    node_1 expects answers ["Antragsteller volljährig holds for case 1"] and any unknowns.
    not_node_1 expects answers ["it is not the case that Antragsteller volljährig holds for case 1"] and any unknowns.

scenario generated_3 is, as stated in "age-check.ruml" at generated_3:
    % dp_age is 17
    the Alter des Antragstellers of case 1 is 17.
    node_1 expects answers [].
    not_node_1 expects answers ["it is not the case that Antragsteller volljährig holds for case 1"].

scenario generated_4 is, as stated in "age-check.ruml" at generated_4:
    % dp_age is 19
    the Alter des Antragstellers of case 1 is 19.
    node_1 expects answers ["Antragsteller volljährig holds for case 1"] and any unknowns.
    not_node_1 expects answers [].

query node_1 is:
    Antragsteller volljährig holds for case 1.

query not_node_1 is:
    it is not the case that Antragsteller volljährig holds for case 1.

